language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Complete an ISBN-13 by filling in the unknown digits (-1 in the input) so that it starts with 978 or 979 and has a valid check digit.
given isbn_init : matrix indexed by [int(1..13)] of int(-1..9)
find isbn : matrix indexed by [int(1..13)] of int(0..9)

branching on [isbn]

such that
$ the known digits of the input are kept
forAll i : int(1..13) . ((isbn_init[i] != -1) -> (isbn[i] = isbn_init[i])),
$ an ISBN-13 starts with 978 or 979
(isbn[1] = 9) /\ (isbn[2] = 7) /\ ((isbn[3] = 8) \/ (isbn[3] = 9)),
$ the check digit: the first 12 digits weighted alternately by 1 and 3, plus the 13th digit, sum to a multiple of 10
((sum i : int(1..6) . (isbn[2*i-1] + 3 * isbn[2*i])) + isbn[13]) % 10 = 0
